From: GameShellNeo project
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: preserve queued TX polling status failures

Publish failed status reads before releasing the host so the caller can
quarantine the worker. Recheck prior error ownership under the host claim;
packet completion can race a separately claimed IRQ failure. Preserve
completed packets, queued ownership and successful status handling.
Candidate only; image integration and hardware qualification remain separate.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/sdio.c
@@ -2496,11 +2496,17 @@
 		if (!bus->intr) {
 			/* Check device status, signal pending interrupt */
 			sdio_claim_host(bus->sdiodev->func1);
-			intstatus = brcmf_sdiod_readl(bus->sdiodev,
-						      intstat_addr, &ret);
+			/* An IRQ may have failed while packet completion ran. */
+			ret = READ_ONCE(bus->sdiodev->io_error);
+			if (!ret) {
+				intstatus = brcmf_sdiod_readl(bus->sdiodev,
+							      intstat_addr, &ret);
+				bus->sdcnt.f2txdata++;
+				if (ret)
+					WRITE_ONCE(bus->sdiodev->io_error, ret);
+			}
 			sdio_release_host(bus->sdiodev->func1);
 
-			bus->sdcnt.f2txdata++;
 			if (ret != 0)
 				break;
 			if (intstatus & bus->hostintmask)
